==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|NL.|en}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|urée|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|οὖρον||urine|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|biochemistry|lang=en}} A water-soluble [[organic compound]], CO(NH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>2</sub>, formed by the [[metabolism]] of [[protein]]s and excreted in the [[urine]].
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} Any ''N''-[[substituted]] [[derivative]] of urea, with the general formula (R<sub>1</sub>R<sub>2</sub>N)CO(NR<sub>3</sub>R<sub>4</sub>).

====Synonyms====
* {{l/en|carbamide}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l/en|polyurea}}
* {{l/en|urea-formaldehyde resin}}

